<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Can German auto manufacturing recover after Mercedes and VW cuts?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea7283162a1d72a227bf2c93c8b122d5e35b791ff264512a2567ea07f5312e26</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928--88277c189f1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German automakers are pulling back on investments at home, sparking fresh anxiety about the auto sector's future. Some industry watchers think there is still a narrow window to stem the decline. But how?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Measles in America: Here's a constructive approach to beating the highly contagious disease, based on Brazil's experience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10dc553e0a85ad34698222aef1b70c8c977e650bd1f7715abb831b68daf47fde</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/measles-in-america-here-s-a-constructive-approach-to-beating-the-highly-contagious-disease-based-on-/a-79990626--0bf8150cfd5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/measles-in-america-here-s-a-constructive-approach-to-beating-the-highly-contagious-disease-based-on-brazil-s-experience/a-79990626?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is now officially a measles contagion zone. By mid-2026, there were more infections than in all of the previous year. But it could beat measles again, just like Brazil did two years ago.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Is Pakistan backing anti-Taliban groups in Afghanistan?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8dd5d76cf33fa21024e2b0f7ff093d9490d3f7d2a3338f011e21f2c9ba60af3</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814--1a7b1c3175b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban rulers in Afghanistan have accused Pakistan of aiding and sheltering armed resistance groups. The allegations come amid heightened tensions and are likely to deepen the rift between the two neighbors.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany face belgium in Nations League quarterfinals — Klopp plays down favorites tag</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7be7875e7fe7accfdd634856302ddbdad9d98eadf475a226c997daebd43956a2</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-face-belgium-in-nations-league-quarterfinals-klopp-plays-down-favorites-tag/a-80004794--66b2cbbf524d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-face-belgium-in-nations-league-quarterfinals-klopp-plays-down-favorites-tag/a-80004794?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp is looking to "carry positive momentum forward" as his team draw neighboring Belgium in the quarterfinals of the UEFA Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU and UK strike 'landmark deal' to strengthen ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a114ded39193531a023854eadd0fd9e16f638486e6ca477a6b3c553ee71014</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076--f12586fcea84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union and the United Kingdom have agreed on "landmark" deals on youth mobility and trade. Leaders on both sides praised the agreement as they seek to rebuild ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey takes control of opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61260c3c33e01a414896624be28a99d8de5635cbb725fd1ccff35dc7f8b3189b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984--d9f6e0119d22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest in a series of raids and arrests, another major pro-opposition Turkish broadcaster has been brought under state control. This is the third in a year.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa at COP31: Will climate cash finally flow?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36ffa818af23249d3f9b84c4274cdf871249eb612e395a66c49e60dc44095d9d</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-at-cop31-will-climate-cash-finally-flow/a-80002269--5d2b279256b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-at-cop31-will-climate-cash-finally-flow/a-80002269?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the curtains draw to a close on COP31 in Antalya, one question looms large for African countries: will climate promises finally translate into the funding African communities need to cope with a warming world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar genocide ruling: Rohingya say struggle for justice not over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a2b6e9761bd0ec7811588ce4dfc390aa591c977ed265bc3361b78aaee52396a</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365--347a55d37759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ has held Myanmar responsible for genocide against the Rohingya and ordered restitution and reparations. Community members have hailed the ruling, but caution that achieving real change will be long and hard.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:242e6ce00f420a5c7e7a58398e3067880e047320fbad72e2da3b279cad7b23dc</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Russian attack 'one of largest,' Zelenskyy says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc4ec46be2893fe6daecb5f2fcc376ffce091a8519dd4a055c9eb2106980aeaa</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russian-attack-one-of-largest-zelenskyy-says/live-79999822--2e1dfbc4ab78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russian-attack-one-of-largest-zelenskyy-says/live-79999822?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy said Russia launched one of the largest aerial attacks since the invasion began. Poland accused Moscow of a "provocation" after two missiles likely landed in the NATO country. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: UN Climate summit enters final phase with no deal in sight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db368272f761f530843b5ebf30aec9886dbb75893b5375c9d66e7eca1a1d802c</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-un-climate-summit-enters-final-phase-with-no-deal-in-sight/live-79999516--9cd590b81239.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-un-climate-summit-enters-final-phase-with-no-deal-in-sight/live-79999516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After nearly two weeks of negotiations, countries remain divided on how to fight global warming. A new draft declaration doesn't mention the phaseout of fossil fuels, the main drivers of climate change. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lufthansa to cut 1,000 jobs, citing ongoing losses — reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:488783731b64d0e858fdbb73f53cab8e2114e8f5ab99767ecc09934958819579</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062--a7b4260396ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a letter obtained by the media, Lufthansa's executive board said the German company is losing €20 million every month. In addition to job cuts, operational cuts are also planned.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Have we missed our chance to stop climate change?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f63fc375381ee7eba370cda1c99ab959138bb6b8cf491d61f9992d4e38d8a7c0</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199--68173e73a2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From record-breaking heat to devastating floods and wildfires, the warning signs are everywhere. Can rising temperatures still be brought under control?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>India: Pakistani minister visits Delhi for SCO forum amid frozen ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d08047ce26792ac0c7f2432012e9d8ae59622afe4643488b1ee6119f97239dc5</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-pakistani-minister-visits-delhi-for-sco-forum-amid-frozen-ties/live-79999264--d096d9f0fd84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-pakistani-minister-visits-delhi-for-sco-forum-amid-frozen-ties/live-79999264?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan's Climate Minister Musadik Malik has arrived in New Delhi for an SCO cultural forum, the first visit by a Pakistani federal minister since 2023. Meanwhile, Cyclone Akvan has made landfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi praises 'turnaround' in relationship with Australia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34855b28acc8bea27ee0dbef5ff4946898f8e99d4cc57c4e666dc9c6682c34ef</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-praises-turnaround-in-relationship-with-australia/a-79999229--091456c7e1ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-praises-turnaround-in-relationship-with-australia/a-79999229?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The leaders of Australia and China have held talks on sidelines of APEC summit. Australian PM Anthony Albanese is also slated to meet Chinese Premier Li Qiang.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz joins German-Ukrainian business forum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976d6449c2db73f380ccad3bfe937bbdaae78a58f77db5c34a7fbb1427aa49dd</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-joins-german-ukrainian-business-forum/live-79998529--9b4daddd11c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-joins-german-ukrainian-business-forum/live-79998529?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Merz is taking part in a forum to boost business ties with Ukraine. Meanwhile, youth protests are expected to take to the streets again. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>White House replaces cyber security chief after tech outages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7f3bd468e4156d107c3206943ae1ad2e512fa9e7786d8b909e11aeb7ccb3887</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T04:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/white-house-replaces-cyber-security-chief-after-tech-outages/a-79998531--9eac64988758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/white-house-replaces-cyber-security-chief-after-tech-outages/a-79998531?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sean Cairncross is leaving his role as national cyber director after a chaotic week of tech outages. Kirsten Davies, the Pentagon's chief information officer, will assume the position in an acting capacity.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New Ukraine talks including Europe to be held 'soon' — Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa0bdece9f6d10b16558e4aad8c0807a2cc56fd8a3c04a425378ec04f2e0c3f1</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T01:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-ukraine-talks-including-europe-to-be-held-soon-merz/a-79997961--25ea534d77af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-ukraine-talks-including-europe-to-be-held-soon-merz/a-79997961?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's Chancellor Friedrich Merz says European leaders could take part in fresh Ukraine talks on "neutral ground." The UK and EU countries have urged a seat at the table in meetings between the US, Russia and Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cincinnati's famous hippo Fiona dies after eating visitor's hat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4233991bd36e78c9ff23190ac01fe8bdb6330c2e2e20c5a241d79b5751397e8f</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T01:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cincinnati-s-famous-hippo-fiona-dies-after-eating-visitor-s-hat/a-79998371--c1abf377d83b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cincinnati-s-famous-hippo-fiona-dies-after-eating-visitor-s-hat/a-79998371?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fiona was a global sensation at the Cincinnati Zoo in the US. The hippo, who was born prematurely, was named after the "Shrek" film character.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Price tag for US war in Iran barrels past $48 billion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:065a493473d4bca7937ec881de4bfe4984636168a2e0133fcf79d9365d6876f1</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T23:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/price-tag-for-us-war-in-iran-barrels-past-48-billion/a-79998255--730de4605f63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/price-tag-for-us-war-in-iran-barrels-past-48-billion/a-79998255?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pentagon budget officer has said the price of the Iran war surpassed $48.3 billion last week. That does not include costs sustained in Iranian attacks on US bases — lawmakers want details the Pentagon is loath to give.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Putin proposes second humanitarian ceasefire — is it a trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c71ead57d2df1f847be99a1a5968c8b6d1e64bae6f39e33a0e84b598d1146dd6</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772--e715071e3f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian President Putin has suggested evacuating civilians from the embattled Ukrainian city of Kostiantynivka. But experts warn this could serve military, not humanitarian, aims. What should Kyiv do?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
